            "english_quote": "may be able to burn things away in opposition to desire.",
            "issue": "The draft makes opposition to desire qualify the consuming action. The supplied sequence τὰ κατὰ τῆς ἐπιθυμίας instead directly supports a substantivized prepositional phrase: 'the things against desire.' The draft's alternative attachment requires τὰ to function independently as an elliptical object, but neither the sentence nor the note identifies a recoverable substantive that supports the indefinite English 'things.' The note honestly discloses the difficulty, but contextual preference alone does not substantiate this syntactic reassignment. The problem is the unsupported main rendering, not merely the existence of competing interpretations or an unverified printed reading.",
